WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:06.040
Causematch matches people with nonprofits across Los Angeles County that need a hand.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:10.400
Here's how a new nonprofit and a new volunteer find each other.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.076
First, a nonprofit joins.

00:00:13.076 --> 00:00:20.390
Jordan, from Silver Lake Garden Friends, asks for access with the organization's name and tax ID.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:25.902
A Causematch admin reviews the request and approves it in one tap.

00:00:25.902 --> 00:00:28.760
Jordan gets an email with a sign-in link.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.732
There's no password to remember.

00:00:31.732 --> 00:00:36.890
Jordan enters their email, opens the link, and lands on an empty dashboard.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:41.306
Jordan says the nonprofit can confirm volunteer hours.

00:00:41.306 --> 00:00:49.410
Then Jordan posts an opening: what volunteers will do, where and when, how long it lasts, and how many people they need.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:03.899
Now, a volunteer.

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:08.890
Riley signs up with a phone number and the six-digit code we text them.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:15.810
One short form: a first name, where Riley will help from, and how much they care about each cause.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:25.195
In preferences, under When, Riley ticks the times they're usually free.

00:01:25.195 --> 00:01:26.470
These stay private.

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:36.304
The deck ranks openings for Riley, and each card says why it's shown.

00:01:36.304 --> 00:01:38.833
Jordan's garden opening is right here.

00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:40.260
Riley taps the heart.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:47.597
On Jordan's side, the inbox badge goes up.

00:01:47.597 --> 00:01:50.950
Riley appears with only what they chose to share.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:52.750
Jordan accepts.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.750
The first shift is booked, and a chat opens.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:01.950
Riley sees it's a match, reads Jordan's message, and replies.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:11.240
The reply arrives live, and Jordan's dashboard flags it as a message to answer.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:16.890
And the shift is on Jordan's schedule, ready to mark attended once it happens.

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:20.105
A few days later, the shift is done.

00:02:20.105 --> 00:02:25.270
Jordan marks Riley as attended in one tap, with the hours already filled in.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:34.880
Riley opens Me, then Shifts and hours, and sees the hours the nonprofit confirmed: the shift, the nonprofit, and who confirmed them.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:42.766
In preferences, under Causes and places, Riley can choose to see the nonprofits that confirm hours first.

00:02:42.766 --> 00:02:45.330
Their cards say, Confirms your hours.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:49.853
Causematch.

00:02:49.853 --> 00:02:51.530
Swipe to volunteer.
